---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
import versionText from "../../../VERSION?raw";

const canonical = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
const ogImage = new URL("/og-image.png", Astro.site);
const version = versionText.trim();
const releaseTag = `v${version}`;
const description =
  "A small .agents workspace for durable AI coding work: work items, research notes, execution-ready plans, verification evidence, and optional handoffs across threads.";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6f2" />
    <title>dot-agents — AI-ready agent workspace</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />

    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:title" content="dot-agents — AI-ready agent workspace" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="dot-agents — Make AI coding work survive the next thread" />

    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="dot-agents — AI-ready agent workspace" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />
    <meta name="twitter:image:alt" content="dot-agents — Make AI coding work survive the next thread" />

    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

    <div class="page-shell">
      <SiteHeader />

      <main id="main-content">
        <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <h1 id="hero-title">Make AI coding work <em>survive the next thread.</em></h1>
            <p class="hero-description">
              Small changes stay conversational. When continuity matters, dot-agents stores work items, plans, and
              verification in your repo’s plain <code>.agents/</code> folder so the next thread can continue.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button button-primary" href="#install">Install with one command <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="install" class="install-section" aria-labelledby="install-title">
          <div class="install-intro">
            <h2 id="install-title">Add it to your repo.</h2>
            <p>
              Run this from your repository root. It creates <code>AGENTS.md</code> and <code>.agents/</code>, and
              preserves your work when you sync.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="install-panel">
            <div class="terminal">
              <div class="terminal-bar">
                <span class="terminal-label"><i></i> terminal — repo root</span>
                <span>bash</span>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-command">
                <pre><code><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span> <span id="install-command">curl -fsSL https://<wbr />raw.githubusercontent.com/colmarius/<wbr />dot-agents/main/install.sh | bash</span></code></pre>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-hints">
                <p><span>Review</span><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colmarius/dot-agents/main/install.sh | less</code></p>
                <p><span>Pin {releaseTag}</span><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colmarius/dot-agents/main/install.sh | bash -s -- --ref {releaseTag}</code></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="install-next">Then tell your agent: <code>Run adapt</code>.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="workflow" class="workflow-section section-block" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">Choose the smallest useful path</p>
            <h2 id="workflow-title">Keep simple work simple. Make durable work resumable.</h2>
            <p>
              Stay in the conversation when one thread is enough. Open a work item only when continuity,
              coordination, decisions, or a handoff makes repository context worth maintaining.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Explore workflow guides <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>

          <div class="workflow-map">
            <p class="workflow-choice"><span>Request or change</span></p>

            <div class="workflow-paths">
              <article class="workflow-path workflow-path-conversational" aria-labelledby="conversational-path-title">
                <header class="workflow-path-header">
                  <p class="path-kicker">Self-contained</p>
                  <h3 id="conversational-path-title">Stay in this conversation</h3>
                  <p>Use no repository workflow artifacts when the scope is clear and one conversation is enough.</p>
                </header>

                <ol class="workflow-steps">
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">01</span>
                    <h4>Work directly</h4>
                    <p>Plan only as needed, then implement from the request in this conversation.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">02</span>
                    <h4>Verify</h4>
                    <p>Run checks that match the change’s risk.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">03</span>
                    <h4>Report</h4>
                    <p>Summarize the outcome and any remaining uncertainty.</p>
                  </li>
                </ol>
              </article>

              <article class="workflow-path workflow-path-durable" aria-labelledby="durable-path-title">
                <header class="workflow-path-header">
                  <p class="path-kicker">Continuity has value</p>
                  <h3 id="durable-path-title">Create durable context</h3>
                  <p>Use a work item when work must resume, coordinate, preserve decisions, or move between threads.</p>
                </header>

                <ol class="workflow-steps">
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">01</span>
                    <h4>Work item</h4>
                    <p><code>index.md</code> owns status and the exact next action.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">02 · optional</span>
                    <h4>Context</h4>
                    <p>Add research or requirements only when unknowns need them.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">03 · optional</span>
                    <h4>Plan when useful</h4>
                    <p>Define scoped tasks when execution needs sequencing.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">04</span>
                    <h4>Execute</h4>
                    <p>Implement in the current thread by default.</p>
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <span class="workflow-step-number">05</span>
                    <h4>Evidence and closeout</h4>
                    <p>Record proof, promote reusable lessons, commit the final snapshot, then remove the work item.</p>
                  </li>
                </ol>

                <aside class="workflow-handoff" aria-label="Optional handoff path">
                  <p class="path-kicker">Optional branch</p>
                  <h4>Hand off when useful</h4>
                  <p>Prepare bounded context only when another worker, thread, or environment genuinely helps; persist it only when reuse adds value.</p>
                </aside>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="artifacts-section section-block" aria-labelledby="artifacts-title">
          <div class="section-heading section-heading-split">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">What lands in your repo</p>
              <h2 id="artifacts-title">Plain files. One place to resume.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="section-aside">
              <p>A new thread reads <code>index.md</code>, then loads only the plan, research, or progress it needs.</p>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://with-agents.dev/coding/posts/durable-context-coding-agents/">
                Why durable context? <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="artifact-grid">
            <div class="file-tree" role="group" aria-label="Files added by dot-agents">
              <div class="file-tree-header">
                <span>your-project/</span>
                <span>tracked</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>├── <b>AGENTS.md</b>       <span># project instructions</span>
└── <b>.agents/</b>
    ├── <b>work/</b>       <span># durable work items</span>
    ├── <b>research/</b>   <span># reusable findings</span>
    ├── <b>references/</b> <span># local reference repos</span>
    ├── <b>skills/</b>     <span># repeatable workflows</span>
    └── <b>scripts/</b>    <span># safe sync updates</span></code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="example-document">
              <div class="document-bar"><span>work/feature/user-authentication/index.md</span><span>● saved</span></div>
              <pre><code><b># User authentication</b>

Status: planned
Category: feature
Updated: 2026-06-22

<b>## Why</b>
Users need secure access across sessions.

<b>## Summary</b>
Add auth flows and session persistence.

<b>## Next Action</b>
Implement Task 1 from plan.md.</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="commands-section section-block" aria-labelledby="commands-title">
          <div class="commands-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow">Start with these prompts</p>
            <h2 id="commands-title">Ask for what you need.</h2>
            <p>Use these prompts as written. Add detail only when it helps.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="command-list">
            <article>
              <code>Run adapt</code>
              <p>Fill <code>AGENTS.md</code> with the repo’s commands and conventions.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <code>Create a new work item for ...</code>
              <p>Start durable context under <code>.agents/work/</code>.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <code>Create a plan for ...</code>
              <p>Plan conversationally, or turn durable context into implementation-ready tasks.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <code>Write a handoff prompt for ...</code>
              <p>Prepare a scoped prompt when another thread would help.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="companion-section section-block" aria-labelledby="companion-title">
          <a class="companion-card" href="https://with-agents.dev/coding/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <div class="companion-copy">
              <header class="companion-brand">
                <span class="companion-wordmark">with-agents</span>
                <span class="companion-badge">Companion field guide</span>
              </header>

              <h2 id="companion-title">Go deeper on the practice behind the workflow.</h2>
              <p>
                dot-agents keeps durable work in the repo. With Agents is the source-backed field guide to briefing
                coding agents, spotting AI slop, preserving context, demanding evidence, and coordinating useful work.
              </p>
              <span class="companion-cta">
                Explore with-agents.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <aside class="companion-index" aria-label="Topics covered by With Agents">
              <p>Practical coding-agent workflows</p>
              <ul>
                <li><span>01</span> Briefs and context</li>
                <li><span>02</span> Quality and proof</li>
                <li><span>03</span> Coordination and outcomes</li>
              </ul>
            </aside>
          </a>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer class="site-footer">
        <a class="wordmark footer-wordmark" href="/" aria-label="dot-agents home"><span><b>.</b>agents</span></a>
        <p>Durable context for AI coding agents.</p>
        <nav aria-label="Footer navigation">
          <a href="https://github.com/colmarius/dot-agents/blob/main/QUICKSTART.md">Quickstart</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/colmarius/dot-agents/blob/main/docs/migration-v0.5.md">v0.5 migration</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/colmarius/dot-agents/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md">Changelog</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/colmarius/dot-agents">GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://ampcode.com">Made for Amp + AI agents</a>
          <span>MIT License</span>
        </nav>
      </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
      import { addCopyControl } from "../scripts/copy-controls";

      const container = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".terminal-command");
      const command = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#install-command");

      if (container && command) addCopyControl(container, command, "install command");
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
